{"archetypes":[{"name":"ci-pipeline","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds Python CI jobs and local Makefile/relevant-checks wiring that must align with ship-pr job classification.","prompt_body":"Investigate the workflow, Makefile, relevant-checks, and ci-failed-jobs integration for the new Python lint and test jobs. Check job names, dependency caching, working directories, setup-node usage, and local check selection for drift between CI and developer paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"python-foundation","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The new flat Python tree establishes contracts later phases will depend on, so API and boundary mistakes compound.","prompt_body":"Review the new Python runtime modules as a cohesive foundation for later ship-pr migration phases. Focus on dataclass immutability, injected runner seams, stdlib-only boundaries, flat import assumptions, and whether public APIs match the intended phase-one surface. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"process-retry","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Subprocess, retry, gh/git, and launcher wrappers encode behavior that can silently diverge from the shell implementation.","prompt_body":"Inspect subprocess execution, retry policy, gh/git wrappers, and agent launcher behavior for command construction, timeout handling, idempotency, and transient classification. Look for cases where captured output, return codes, retries, or parsed records diverge from the shell parity described by the plan. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"redaction-parity","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The redaction module replaces security-critical shell behavior and needs focused parity review beyond generic security scanning.","prompt_body":"Examine the redaction implementation and tests against the planned bash parity for secret families, PEM private-key truncation, tmpdir and operator-path rewrites, and idempotence. Treat both leakage and over-broad rewriting as security-sensitive regressions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"strangler-boundary","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan promises no live /implement behavior change except CI job recognition, but the diff touches shell integration paths.","prompt_body":"Check whether changes touching ship-pr, ci-failed-jobs, relevant checks, docs, and Python wiring preserve the planned strangler boundary. Verify the new Python tree remains dev and CI only, while live /implement orchestration does not accidentally import, invoke, or depend on it beyond recognized CI job names. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
